1
00:00:00,290 --> 00:00:02,720
If your knee replacement
still hurts

2
00:00:02,720 --> 00:00:05,190
and the X-ray keeps coming
back fine,

3
00:00:05,190 --> 00:00:06,450
don't accept that.

4
00:00:06,770 --> 00:00:08,360
I've been installing
countertops

5
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:09,620
for thirty years.

6
00:00:09,730 --> 00:00:12,020
Carrying heavy stone slabs
and kneeling

7
00:00:12,020 --> 00:00:13,430
at cabinets all day.

8
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:14,750
I had my right knee

9
00:00:14,750 --> 00:00:16,540
replaced two years ago.

10
00:00:16,730 --> 00:00:19,000
It has hurt every day
since.

11
00:00:19,560 --> 00:00:20,900
Not surgery pain.

12
00:00:20,940 --> 00:00:22,180
I know what that felt
like,

13
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:23,000
and it went away.

14
00:00:23,040 --> 00:00:24,130
This is different.

15
00:00:24,170 --> 00:00:24,580
Tight.

16
00:00:24,620 --> 00:00:25,190
Full.

17
00:00:25,230 --> 00:00:26,150
Like a band around

18
00:00:26,150 --> 00:00:27,880
the joint that never
loosens.

19
00:00:27,940 --> 00:00:29,050
And for two years I've

20
00:00:29,050 --> 00:00:30,610
been told the same thing.

21
00:00:30,770 --> 00:00:32,040
Give it time.

22
00:00:32,380 --> 00:00:34,960
At six weeks it was
swelling,

23
00:00:34,960 --> 00:00:36,340
and swelling is normal.

24
00:00:36,510 --> 00:00:37,320
At three months,

25
00:00:37,320 --> 00:00:38,480
give it six.

26
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:39,330
At six months,

27
00:00:39,330 --> 00:00:41,030
some knees take a full
year.

28
00:00:41,290 --> 00:00:42,080
At a year,

29
00:00:42,080 --> 00:00:44,010
eighteen months isn't
unusual.

30
00:00:44,130 --> 00:00:45,100
And I didn't just wait.

31
00:00:45,140 --> 00:00:46,550
We went down the list.

32
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:48,010
More physical therapy.

33
00:00:48,220 --> 00:00:49,450
Every session,

34
00:00:49,450 --> 00:00:51,030
every exercise at home.

35
00:00:51,400 --> 00:00:52,520
I got stronger.

36
00:00:52,560 --> 00:00:53,860
The tightness never moved.

37
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:55,600
The pain pills helped,

38
00:00:55,600 --> 00:00:56,860
and that was the problem.

39
00:00:56,900 --> 00:00:58,760
I'm already on enough
every morning,

40
00:00:58,760 --> 00:00:59,860
and nobody could tell me

41
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:00,790
when I'd get to stop.

42
00:01:00,830 --> 00:01:02,100
Then a nerve block.

43
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:04,440
Then talk of burning the
nerve.

44
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:06,010
And after that, a second

45
00:01:06,010 --> 00:01:07,220
operation to go back

46
00:01:07,220 --> 00:01:08,390
in and do it over.

47
00:01:08,660 --> 00:01:09,640
I said no.

48
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:11,570
Every morning I stepped
out of bed

49
00:01:11,570 --> 00:01:12,610
and my knee felt like

50
00:01:12,610 --> 00:01:14,210
a band was wrapped around
it,

51
00:01:14,210 --> 00:01:16,750
tightening every inch I
tried to straighten.

52
00:01:16,960 --> 00:01:18,230
Every morning I took
something

53
00:01:18,230 --> 00:01:19,720
for it and went to work.

54
00:01:19,810 --> 00:01:21,190
Couldn't do the stairs,

55
00:01:21,190 --> 00:01:22,350
couldn't stand at the
counter

56
00:01:22,350 --> 00:01:24,020
long enough to finish
dinner,

57
00:01:24,020 --> 00:01:26,100
couldn't sit through my
granddaughter's game

58
00:01:26,100 --> 00:01:28,420
without shifting every two
minutes.

59
00:01:28,570 --> 00:01:29,470
At work,

60
00:01:29,470 --> 00:01:31,100
the young guys on my crew
started

61
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:32,760
carrying my end of the
slab.

62
00:01:32,990 --> 00:01:34,450
Nobody said anything.

63
00:01:34,700 --> 00:01:35,970
It woke me at night,

64
00:01:35,970 --> 00:01:37,560
and it turned ordinary
things,

65
00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:38,690
like getting in the truck

66
00:01:38,690 --> 00:01:40,280
or up off the floor,

67
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:41,440
into a decision.

68
00:01:41,670 --> 00:01:42,930
After a long and serious

69
00:01:42,930 --> 00:01:43,910
talk with my wife,

70
00:01:43,910 --> 00:01:45,880
I went back in one more
time.

71
00:01:46,320 --> 00:01:47,410
That was the fourth set

72
00:01:47,410 --> 00:01:48,920
of X-rays on this knee.

73
00:01:49,130 --> 00:01:50,630
And like the three before
it,

74
00:01:50,630 --> 00:01:53,110
the answer was everything
looks great.

75
00:01:53,150 --> 00:01:55,030
No loosening, no
infection,

76
00:01:55,030 --> 00:01:55,890
nothing wrong.

77
00:01:56,090 --> 00:01:57,240
Only this time

78
00:01:57,240 --> 00:01:59,160
there was no new number.

79
00:01:59,210 --> 00:02:01,250
Nobody said give it
another six months.

80
00:02:01,290 --> 00:02:03,210
There was nothing left to
give it.

81
00:02:03,600 --> 00:02:04,590
I sat in the parking

82
00:02:04,590 --> 00:02:05,530
lot for a while.

83
00:02:05,570 --> 00:02:06,540
Okay, I thought.

84
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:07,840
Then explain this.

85
00:02:08,140 --> 00:02:10,250
Anyway, a couple of months
back,

86
00:02:10,250 --> 00:02:11,720
I hit my breaking point.

87
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:14,090
It was around 2:30 in the
morning.

88
00:02:14,290 --> 00:02:16,260
Everyone in the house was
asleep

89
00:02:16,260 --> 00:02:18,010
and I was downstairs in
the recliner

90
00:02:18,010 --> 00:02:19,130
with my leg up,

91
00:02:19,130 --> 00:02:20,780
trying to find any angle
where

92
00:02:20,780 --> 00:02:21,900
it didn't feel like
something

93
00:02:21,900 --> 00:02:24,450
was wrapped around my knee
and tightening.

94
00:02:24,770 --> 00:02:27,090
My wife didn't know I'd
come downstairs.

95
00:02:27,270 --> 00:02:28,950
By then I'd stopped
telling her.

96
00:02:29,210 --> 00:02:29,990
I had a kitchen

97
00:02:29,990 --> 00:02:31,240
to install at seven.

98
00:02:31,620 --> 00:02:32,610
And I just thought,

99
00:02:32,610 --> 00:02:34,450
is this really my life
now?

100
00:02:34,490 --> 00:02:36,000
I can't live like this.

101
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:37,760
Thirty years of
countertops,

102
00:02:37,760 --> 00:02:38,680
and I couldn't see how

103
00:02:38,680 --> 00:02:40,030
I'd get through one more.

104
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:42,040
So I made myself a
promise.

105
00:02:42,260 --> 00:02:43,180
I wouldn't go a day

106
00:02:43,180 --> 00:02:44,690
without looking for an
answer.

107
00:02:45,050 --> 00:02:46,060
And when I found one,

108
00:02:46,060 --> 00:02:47,250
I'd share it with everyone

109
00:02:47,250 --> 00:02:48,670
going through the same
thing.

110
00:02:49,090 --> 00:02:50,170
So I got my laptop

111
00:02:50,170 --> 00:02:51,350
out and went looking.

112
00:02:51,610 --> 00:02:52,770
Not for a product.

113
00:02:52,810 --> 00:02:53,960
For an explanation.

114
00:02:54,340 --> 00:02:55,750
Mayo Clinic forums,

115
00:02:55,750 --> 00:02:57,770
the knee replacement group
on Facebook,

116
00:02:57,770 --> 00:02:59,890
doctor videos, medical
animations.

117
00:03:00,160 --> 00:03:01,580
And that's when I found a
video

118
00:03:01,580 --> 00:03:03,390
from a physical therapist
named Dr.

119
00:03:03,430 --> 00:03:04,750
Steven Salinger,

120
00:03:04,750 --> 00:03:06,250
whose own wife had been

121
00:03:06,250 --> 00:03:07,640
through exactly this.

122
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:09,780
But before I say anything
else,

123
00:03:09,780 --> 00:03:11,240
I want to be straight with
you.

124
00:03:11,630 --> 00:03:13,990
You've already had
something work fast.

125
00:03:14,070 --> 00:03:14,910
The ice.

126
00:03:14,950 --> 00:03:16,660
The first week of a new
pill.

127
00:03:16,780 --> 00:03:18,570
The good day after a
session.

128
00:03:18,610 --> 00:03:19,900
Then it wore off.

129
00:03:19,950 --> 00:03:21,990
That's the part nobody
warns you about.

130
00:03:22,150 --> 00:03:23,810
Fast relief isn't relief.

131
00:03:23,980 --> 00:03:24,930
It's a preview.

132
00:03:25,340 --> 00:03:26,250
So I'm not going to tell

133
00:03:26,250 --> 00:03:27,330
you this works fast.

134
00:03:27,370 --> 00:03:28,230
It doesn't.

135
00:03:28,430 --> 00:03:30,220
But if you're willing to
be patient,

136
00:03:30,220 --> 00:03:31,060
and to look at what's

137
00:03:31,060 --> 00:03:32,780
going on around your new
knee

138
00:03:32,780 --> 00:03:34,440
instead of inside it,
there

139
00:03:34,440 --> 00:03:36,840
is a real reason it still
hurts.

140
00:03:36,950 --> 00:03:38,710
And something you can do
about it.

141
00:03:38,830 --> 00:03:40,530
Let me explain what he
said,

142
00:03:40,530 --> 00:03:41,760
because this is what
changed

143
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:42,720
everything for me.

144
00:03:42,760 --> 00:03:44,410
He started with the
basics.

145
00:03:44,560 --> 00:03:45,850
A knee replacement takes
out

146
00:03:45,850 --> 00:03:47,290
the worn joint surfaces
and puts

147
00:03:47,290 --> 00:03:48,600
in metal and plastic.

148
00:03:48,810 --> 00:03:50,640
That's what stops the
arthritis pain

149
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:52,170
you had before the
operation.

150
00:03:52,550 --> 00:03:54,080
That part I already knew.

151
00:03:54,450 --> 00:03:55,850
But then he explained
something

152
00:03:55,850 --> 00:03:57,400
nobody had ever told me.

153
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:57,940
He said,

154
00:03:57,940 --> 00:03:59,290
think about a swollen foot

155
00:03:59,290 --> 00:04:00,400
inside a shoe.

156
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:02,080
The shoe didn't shrink.

157
00:04:02,320 --> 00:04:04,640
Your foot is taking up
more room,

158
00:04:04,640 --> 00:04:06,190
so everything feels
cramped

159
00:04:06,190 --> 00:04:07,880
and tight and squeezed.

160
00:04:08,120 --> 00:04:09,970
Your new knee sits in a
limited

161
00:04:09,970 --> 00:04:11,650
space with living tissue

162
00:04:11,650 --> 00:04:12,910
packed all around it.

163
00:04:13,140 --> 00:04:15,000
To put that knee in, the
surgeon

164
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:16,770
had to work through that
tissue.

165
00:04:17,010 --> 00:04:20,210
Afterwards it gets
inflamed and swollen.

166
00:04:20,530 --> 00:04:21,920
At first that's normal.

167
00:04:22,010 --> 00:04:24,040
But in some people that
swelling can

168
00:04:24,040 --> 00:04:27,360
stay switched on far
longer than expected.

169
00:04:27,430 --> 00:04:29,400
And swollen tissue takes
up more

170
00:04:29,400 --> 00:04:31,380
room than calm tissue
does.

171
00:04:31,550 --> 00:04:32,880
So when you bend,

172
00:04:32,880 --> 00:04:34,760
that tissue gets
compressed.

173
00:04:34,950 --> 00:04:36,260
When you straighten,

174
00:04:36,260 --> 00:04:37,520
it gets pulled tight.

175
00:04:37,630 --> 00:04:38,330
That's the band.

176
00:04:38,370 --> 00:04:39,540
That's the ache

177
00:04:39,540 --> 00:04:40,880
that never quite leaves.

178
00:04:40,920 --> 00:04:41,700
And you start being

179
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:42,930
the one who says,

180
00:04:42,930 --> 00:04:43,620
you go ahead.

181
00:04:43,660 --> 00:04:44,620
I'll stay here.

182
00:04:44,940 --> 00:04:46,770
And that's exactly why so
much

183
00:04:46,770 --> 00:04:48,630
of what I'd tried hadn't
worked.

184
00:04:48,990 --> 00:04:51,310
Physical therapy
strengthens the muscles

185
00:04:51,310 --> 00:04:52,280
around the knee.

186
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:53,510
Worth doing,

187
00:04:53,510 --> 00:04:54,410
and I'd done it.

188
00:04:54,620 --> 00:04:56,120
It does nothing about
tissue

189
00:04:56,120 --> 00:04:57,270
taking up room.

190
00:04:57,330 --> 00:04:58,640
A nerve block quiets

191
00:04:58,640 --> 00:05:00,300
the nerve carrying the
signal.

192
00:05:00,580 --> 00:05:02,750
It doesn't touch what's
generating it.

193
00:05:02,960 --> 00:05:04,510
But when that irritated
tissue

194
00:05:04,510 --> 00:05:06,150
finally calms down,

195
00:05:06,150 --> 00:05:07,590
it holds less fluid,

196
00:05:07,590 --> 00:05:09,190
and it takes up less room.

197
00:05:09,410 --> 00:05:11,110
Less room taken up means

198
00:05:11,110 --> 00:05:13,000
less pressure squeezing
the joint.

199
00:05:13,070 --> 00:05:14,790
That's what takes the
pressure off.

200
00:05:15,060 --> 00:05:16,560
After two years of this,

201
00:05:16,560 --> 00:05:18,160
it finally made sense.

202
00:05:18,490 --> 00:05:20,400
The problem was never the
new knee.

203
00:05:20,560 --> 00:05:22,470
It was the tissue crowded
around it.

204
00:05:22,820 --> 00:05:24,350
He calls it the squeeze.

205
00:05:24,450 --> 00:05:26,890
Once you've felt it,
that's the word.

206
00:05:27,170 --> 00:05:29,080
I'd bought knee sleeves,

207
00:05:29,080 --> 00:05:31,910
gel knee pads, compression
braces,

208
00:05:31,910 --> 00:05:34,220
creams, half of Amazon
really,

209
00:05:34,220 --> 00:05:35,250
and all any of it gave

210
00:05:35,250 --> 00:05:36,320
me was an hour.

211
00:05:36,840 --> 00:05:37,750
I even looked at going

212
00:05:37,750 --> 00:05:39,660
to a clinic for the light
therapy.

213
00:05:39,810 --> 00:05:41,850
But at $200 a session

214
00:05:41,850 --> 00:05:43,380
with nothing covered by
insurance,

215
00:05:43,380 --> 00:05:44,900
that was a quick no.

216
00:05:44,970 --> 00:05:46,300
Then one night I went

217
00:05:46,300 --> 00:05:47,570
back to that knee
replacement

218
00:05:47,570 --> 00:05:49,250
group and actually read
it.

219
00:05:49,530 --> 00:05:50,930
Thousands of people,

220
00:05:50,930 --> 00:05:52,780
years out from surgery,

221
00:05:52,780 --> 00:05:54,250
comparing notes on
stiffness

222
00:05:54,250 --> 00:05:56,300
and tightness nobody could
explain.

223
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:58,310
And no matter how far I
scrolled,

224
00:05:58,310 --> 00:06:00,290
the same thing kept coming
up.

225
00:06:00,520 --> 00:06:02,170
This one device,

226
00:06:02,170 --> 00:06:04,100
and people saying it was
the first

227
00:06:04,100 --> 00:06:05,520
thing that made a
difference.

228
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:07,640
And before anyone jumps in
thinking,

229
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:09,440
alright, here it comes,

230
00:06:09,440 --> 00:06:10,950
he's selling me something,

231
00:06:10,950 --> 00:06:12,820
let me shut that down
right now.

232
00:06:13,100 --> 00:06:14,970
I'm only here because I
made myself

233
00:06:14,970 --> 00:06:17,370
a promise at 2:30 in the
morning

234
00:06:17,370 --> 00:06:18,380
that if I ever found

235
00:06:18,380 --> 00:06:19,650
something that helped,

236
00:06:19,650 --> 00:06:20,710
I'd say so.

237
00:06:21,070 --> 00:06:22,920
It's called the KenRelief
Red

238
00:06:22,920 --> 00:06:24,370
Light Therapy Wrap.

239
00:06:24,810 --> 00:06:26,890
At first glance I didn't
buy it.

240
00:06:27,130 --> 00:06:28,760
It looked like the cheap
knee sleeves

241
00:06:28,760 --> 00:06:30,870
off Amazon that did
nothing for me.

242
00:06:31,020 --> 00:06:33,030
But I went to their
website anyway,

243
00:06:33,030 --> 00:06:33,870
just to see what all

244
00:06:33,870 --> 00:06:34,960
the fuss was about.

245
00:06:35,280 --> 00:06:37,140
It's the same red light
therapy clinics

246
00:06:37,140 --> 00:06:39,510
charge $200 a session for,

247
00:06:39,510 --> 00:06:42,250
off machines that cost
fifty thousand dollars,

248
00:06:42,250 --> 00:06:43,190
in a wrap you plug

249
00:06:43,190 --> 00:06:44,360
into the wall at home.

250
00:06:44,420 --> 00:06:46,080
Two hundred and forty
lights.

251
00:06:46,330 --> 00:06:48,280
Red at 660 nanometers

252
00:06:48,280 --> 00:06:50,420
and near-infrared at 850,

253
00:06:50,420 --> 00:06:52,620
run together for the
strongest effect.

254
00:06:52,810 --> 00:06:54,560
Four strength levels.

255
00:06:54,960 --> 00:06:56,780
A five to thirty minute
timer.

256
00:06:56,820 --> 00:06:58,330
Then I saw the guarantee.

257
00:06:58,370 --> 00:06:59,520
Ninety days.

258
00:06:59,590 --> 00:07:02,320
Results or your money
back,

259
00:07:02,320 --> 00:07:04,990
no questions, no store
credit,

260
00:07:04,990 --> 00:07:06,610
and you don't even send it
back.

261
00:07:06,810 --> 00:07:09,210
No physical therapist ever
gave me ninety

262
00:07:09,210 --> 00:07:10,760
days to change my mind.

263
00:07:10,810 --> 00:07:12,450
There wasn't much to lose,

264
00:07:12,450 --> 00:07:13,610
so I ordered it.

265
00:07:13,710 --> 00:07:15,020
Two of them, actually.

266
00:07:15,220 --> 00:07:17,210
Only the right knee was
replaced,

267
00:07:17,210 --> 00:07:19,220
but you favor the leg that
hurts,

268
00:07:19,220 --> 00:07:20,960
and I'd done it for two
years.

269
00:07:21,240 --> 00:07:23,240
The left one was carrying
the difference.

270
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:24,190
When it came,

271
00:07:24,190 --> 00:07:26,270
I strapped it on expecting
nothing,

272
00:07:26,270 --> 00:07:27,340
because I'd been let down

273
00:07:27,340 --> 00:07:29,160
too many times to get
excited.

274
00:07:29,460 --> 00:07:30,950
What I felt was warmth.

275
00:07:30,990 --> 00:07:32,850
Not a heating pad kind of
hot.

276
00:07:32,940 --> 00:07:34,470
More like it was coming
from inside

277
00:07:34,470 --> 00:07:36,040
the knee and spreading
around it.

278
00:07:36,290 --> 00:07:37,330
And that was it.

279
00:07:37,380 --> 00:07:38,900
That was the whole
experience.

280
00:07:38,940 --> 00:07:40,160
When I took it off,

281
00:07:40,160 --> 00:07:41,100
